{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"SIGNING ISSUE HANDED TO /rebar-debug (no assumed root cause). Symptom: 'rebar sign-review <id>' - the documented recovery for a PASS that did not persist - itself fails with {ok:false, signed:false, verdict:PASS, reason:'the attestation could not be persisted: plan review generation remained unstable after 3 attempts'}. Affects 111a-4626-8d2c-42bf, 825c-ba3e-587b-4b7f, 7931-faee-53ba-47b1 (each latest REVIEW_RESULT: verdict PASS, 0 blocking, signature unsigned). Tracebacks: attest.py:202 sign_plan_review -> generation.py:291 sign_manifest -> PlanReviewGenerationError('store-read-failure'); and generation.py:368 -> PlanReviewGenerationRetryable. ~25 rounds of sign-review retry over ~20min recovered none. Prior art, both CLOSED: 790c-a7a3-120a-42c8 (passing review ends unsigned under concurrent writes - its remedy is that sign-review IS the working recovery, which is exactly what fails here) and c083-4d7d-0aca-4e3f (sign-review failing on stray untracked tracker files). CORRECTION TO MY OWN EARLIER CLAIM: I asserted a moving-tickets-HEAD fence as the root cause from reading sign_manifest; that was inference, not evidence, and is NOT to be treated as established."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787370089052309001,"uuid":"5c126ffc-127c-4bd9-b41c-94abc96d4ad2"}